{
  "_notes": [
    "Runtime zoning-district lookup. Each entry points at a jurisdiction's own published",
    "GIS layer -- the only place zoning actually lives, since it is a per-municipality legal",
    "designation and no global geocoder (Google included) carries it.",
    "",
    "district_categories maps the layer's raw zoning code to the coarse vocabulary the source",
    "packs are tagged with. Every mapping below is derived from that city's own ordinance",
    "articles/divisions, not guessed: e.g. blacksburg 'DC' -> mixed-use-core because",
    "'DIVISION 14. - DOWNTOWN COMMERCIAL DISTRICT' is what classification_rules.json maps",
    "DOWNTOWN to. A code that is absent from this map yields a parcel id but no district,",
    "which is the same position we are in today -- never a guess.",
    "",
    "jurisdiction_value guards against a geocode landing on a neighbouring parcel outside the",
    "town limits: a shared county layer serves several jurisdictions, so a row whose",
    "jurisdiction_field does not match is discarded rather than answered with."
  ],
